    "field": "Temperature reconstruction",
    "problem": "Reconstructing pre-instrumental temperatures is challenging due to a lack of direct measurements, necessitating the use of diverse and independent proxies to create robust climate histories and reduce uncertainties in existing multi-proxy models.",
    "method": "We reconstruct annual surface temperatures from 308 glacier length records by deriving temperature changes using a linear response equation and an analytical glacier model that is calibrated on the results of numerical ice flow models.",
    "task": "The task is to reconstruct global and hemispheric surface temperatures for the past 400 years by using historical glacier length fluctuation records from 308 glaciers as an independent temperature proxy.",
